        "Adrian was a Christian who lived in Batanea, a region in southern Syria and Palestine during the Roman period, during the early 4th century AD. Very little is known about his family, upbringing, or life before his martyrdom. He lived at a time when Christianity was still viewed with suspicion by the Roman authorities and when Christians in parts of the empire could face imprisonment, torture, or death for refusing to participate in traditional Roman religious practices. Adrian belonged to the Christian community of Batanea and appears to have been known for his steadfastness and commitment to the Christian faith.",

