      legacy:
        "St. Sabinus of Hermopolis is remembered as an early Egyptian martyr whose life combined Christian charity with steadfastness under persecution. His willingness to use his wealth to assist other Christians demonstrated the importance of practical charity within the early Church, while his refusal to abandon Christ demonstrated the strength of his faith. His story became part of the rich tradition of Egyptian Christian martyrdom that helped shape the spirituality of the early Church. He is honoured particularly as an example for Christians who face pressure, hardship, or persecution because of their faith. His witness reminds Christians that perseverance is strengthened not only by personal courage but also by supporting and encouraging fellow believers during times of trial.",

