      legacy:
        "St. Turibius of Mogrovejo is remembered as one of the great missionary bishops of the Americas and one of the most important Catholic reformers of colonial Peru. His episcopate combined determined defence of Church discipline with a profound concern for the dignity and welfare of indigenous peoples. His extensive pastoral visitations helped bring the sacraments and Christian teaching to communities that had previously received little pastoral care. The reforms associated with the Councils of Lima helped establish a more organised and disciplined Catholic Church throughout Spanish South America, while the seminary he founded contributed to the long-term formation of clergy in the Americas. Turibius became a model of episcopal leadership because he personally experienced the hardships faced by the people he served rather than remaining distant from them. His defence of indigenous peoples also makes him an important witness to the Church's concern for human dignity and justice. He is particularly honoured as a patron of Latin American bishops, missionaries, and indigenous peoples, and his example continues to inspire those involved in evangelisation, pastoral ministry, and the defence of vulnerable communities.",

